  "description": "This course covers the fundamentals of computer graphics, including raster scan display systems, 2D and 3D geometric transformations, and the principles of rendering. Students will study algorithms such as the Bresenham line drawing algorithm, Cohen-Sutherland line clipping, and the Z-buffer algorithm. The course also explores advanced topics like polygon mesh representation, ray tracing, and OpenGL programming. Specific technologies and standards addressed include the OpenGL ES API, WebGL, and the use of shaders for real-time rendering. Students will also analyze the mathematical foundations of computer graphics, including matrix algebra and vector operations, and apply these concepts to create interactive visualizations. The course emphasizes both theoretical understanding and practical implementation through hands-on projects and assignments.",
